   "note": "Designed a block with high symmetry to match the graph connectivity problem. The block uses a translation-invariant ansatz: a uniform single-qubit rotation (RY) followed by a ring of nearest-neighbor CNOTs, a uniform phase shift (RZ), and a ring of next-nearest-neighbor CNOTs. This structure is invariant under cyclic permutation of qubits (generator [1,2,3,4,5,0]), which corresponds to relabeling the graph nodes. Since the feature map encodes edge existence symmetrically, and the target (connectivity) is invariant under node relabeling, this symmetry reduces the parameter space and helps the model generalize to different node labelings of the same graph structure. The use of only 2 parameters per block layer encourages learning global connectivity patterns rather than overfitting to specific edge indices.",
